{"name":"Ground Nutmeg","hex":"#a05a3b","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"ground","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The surface of the Earth, as opposed to the sky or water or underground.","Terrain."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To connect (an electrical conductor or device) to a ground.","To electrocute."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ground"},{"term":"nutmeg","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An evergreen tree (Myristica fragrans) cultivated in the East Indies for its spicy seeds.","The aromatic seed of this tree, used as a spice.\n The powdered seed, ready for use.\n A whole nutmeg seed."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To flavour with nutmeg.","To play the ball between the legs of (an opponent)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/nutmeg"}],"entries":[{"title":"Nutmeg","blocks":[{"text":"Nutmeg is the seed, or the ground spice derived from the seed, of several tree species of the genus Myristica; fragrant nutmeg or true nutmeg is a dark-leaved evergreen tree cultivated for two spices derived from its fruit: nutmeg, from its seed, and mace, from the seed covering. It is also a commercial source of nutmeg essential oil and nutmeg butter. The Banda Islands, in Maluku, Indonesia, are the main producer of nutmeg and mace, and the true nutmeg tree is native to the islands."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c8/Biji_Pala_Bubuk.jpg/330px-Biji_Pala_Bubuk.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nutmeg","wikidata":"Q83165"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/Mace_%28%E0%A6%9C%E0%A6%AF%E0%A6%BC%E0%A6%BF%E0%A6%A4%E0%A7%8D%E0%A6%B0%E0%A6%BF%29.JPG/500px-Mace_%28%E0%A6%9C%E0%A6%AF%E0%A6%BC%E0%A6%BF%E0%A6%A4%E0%A7%8D%E0%A6%B0%E0%A6%BF%29.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikiped